description:
On Wednesday, the House of Representatives advanced a discharge petition and accompanying legislation that would extend Temporary Protected Status (TPS) for Haiti for the next three years.
), reached the 218 signatures required in March to force a vote on Congresswoman Laura Gillen’s (D‑N.Y.)
Four Republicans joined all Democrats in supporting the petition, which allowed the bill to advance without support from the House Republican leadership.
), Congressman Mike Lawler (R-N.Y.), Congresswoman Nicole Malliotakis (R-N.Y.), and Congressman Kevin Kiley (I-Calif.).
In 2025, the Trump administration moved to terminate TPS for Haiti, concluding that the continued presence of Haitian TPS beneficiaries was not in the U.S. national interest.
